MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Google answers a Code Assist account it suspended with 403
PERMISSION_DENIED "This service has been disabled in this account for
violation of Terms of Service." whatever it is asked. 2e58f85e4 reads that
refusal of a request, and rests the account restricted; the account's own
asks are answered with it unseen: its project (loadCodeAssist, on every
start of magpie), its tiers (loadCodeAssist, hourly), its models
(fetchAvailableModels) — asked by discovery, outside the gateway's request
path and its routing, so the suspended account was polled, and refused,
on every start and every hour for good (#5478, the case asked for in
plugins#784).

The judgment is the provider's now (GoogleSuspended), which the gateway
reads its own refusals by; discovery tells the gateway what the vendor
said of the account (DiscoveryRefused), and the gateway rests it at the
write point its own refusals go through (restAfter): the same restricted
rest, keyed as the request path keys one, so the Routing page shows it and
lifts it the same way, restrictedHeld gives the vendor's words to a
request while it rests, and a longer rest standing isn't shortened.
Discovery asks the gateway whether an account rests so
(DiscoveryHeld), and holds its asks while it does: the magpie's hourly ask
of an account's list skips it, Antigravity's pooled listing sends it
nothing and keeps what it listed, and its models, its tiers and its quota
are asked of Google no more until the rest ends or is lifted — then it is
asked again, as the request path asks it.

Run (mote, at this tree on upstream/main d4712e131):
- go test -run 'TestDiscovery' ./internal/provider ./internal/gateway:
  green; without the change (the product files at the parent, the tests
  kept) TestDiscoveryRestsASuspendedAccount is red: the suspended account
  was asked for its list every pass, loadCodeAssist with it, and the
  gateway was told nothing.
- go test -tags nogui ./internal/provider ./internal/gateway: ok
- go vet for darwin, gofmt.

Not tried: a real suspended Google account (the fixture is the reporter's
403 body, in Google's error shape, and their log's shape — loadCodeAssist
refused, fetchAvailableModels still listing); Gemini CLI's own wording of
the same suspension is assumed the same, as 2e58f85e4 did.

